  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A 4-star campsite of the Homair chain in Saint-Aygulf (Fréjus), set between the Argens river and a long natural beach. The official website puts the beach at about 900 metres, along a pedestrian path that runs beside the Villepey ponds.</p>

      <h2>Conditions for your dog</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The campsite's website states "only one dog allowed (excluding categories 1 and 2)" in its services.</li>
        <li>The Fréjus tourist office specifies that animals are accepted.</li>
        <li>The amount of the supplement, the leash rules and the documents required are not published on the pages read: ask the campsite, on 04 95 36 38 37.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the path to the beach runs along a protected natural area (Villepey ponds): keep your dog on a leash on this stretch.</div>

      <h2>To check before you book</h2>
      <p>The amount of the dog supplement, the current rules on Argens beach (see the beach page) and the dates: the 2027 season is announced from 15 May to 31 October.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Base Nature François Léotard and its Pacha beach can be reached from the area, for a change of scenery on your walks.</p>
    </div>

